---
import site from "../../site.config.mjs";
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import LinkPhone from "../components/LinkPhone";
---

<Base title="Setup Guides — Aether" description="How to add an IPTV subscription (Xtream Codes, M3U, Stalker) or a Jellyfin, Emby, Plex, Silo or WebDAV server to Aether, and set up Apple TV from your iPhone.">

    <section class="page-head">
      <div class="wrap">
        <span class="eyebrow">Setup guides</span>
        <h1>Add what you watch.</h1>
        <p class="lede" style="max-width:680px">Aether plays sources you add yourself. Most take under a minute: paste a link, pick a server it found, or sign in with a code.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="docs wrap">
      <nav class="toc" aria-label="On this page">
        <strong>Start</strong>
        <a href="#first-run">Your first source</a>
        <strong>IPTV</strong>
        <a href="#paste-link">Paste a link</a>
        <a href="#xtream">Xtream Codes</a>
        <a href="#m3u">M3U playlist</a>
        <a href="#stalker">Stalker portal</a>
        <a href="#guide">TV guide (XMLTV)</a>
        <strong>Media servers</strong>
        <a href="#find-server">Finding your server</a>
        <a href="#jellyfin">Jellyfin &amp; Emby</a>
        <a href="#quick-connect">Jellyfin Quick Connect</a>
        <a href="#plex">Plex</a>
        <a href="#silo-webdav">Silo &amp; WebDAV</a>
        <strong>More</strong>
        <a href="#apple-tv">Apple TV</a>
        <a href="#services">Trakt, Simkl &amp; more</a>
        <a href="#profiles">Profiles &amp; parental controls</a>
      </nav>

      <div class="prose">
        <div class="notice">
          <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M10.29 3.86 1.82 18a2 2 0 0 0 1.71 3h16.94a2 2 0 0 0 1.71-3L13.71 3.86a2 2 0 0 0-3.42 0zM12 9v4M12 17h.01"/></svg>
          <div>
            <p><strong>Aether includes no channels or content, and we can't recommend where to get any.</strong></p>
            <p class="muted">Add only sources you're entitled to watch. See the <a href="/anti-piracy/">anti-piracy policy</a>.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <section id="first-run">
          <h2>Your first source</h2>
          <p>The first time you open Aether, it asks what you want to watch with:</p>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>IPTV Subscription</strong> — live TV, a guide, movies and series from a provider you pay for.</li>
            <li><strong>Media Server</strong> — your own library on Jellyfin, Emby, Plex, Silo or a WebDAV share.</li>
          </ul>
          <p>Pick one and Aether shows only the fields it needs. You can add more sources of either kind later in <span class="path">Settings → Connections</span>.</p>
          <p>After you add a source, Aether downloads its catalogue and indexes it on your device. A large catalogue can take a few minutes the first time; later updates are much quicker.</p>
        </section>

        <section id="paste-link">
          <h2>Paste your provider's link</h2>
          <p>Providers usually send a link or a login by email. You don't need to know what kind it is — paste it into <strong>Quick Setup</strong> at the top of the IPTV form and Aether works it out:</p>
          <div class="table-wrap">
            <table>
              <thead><tr><th>What you paste</th><th>What Aether does</th></tr></thead>
              <tbody>
                <tr><td>A link with <code>get.php</code> or <code>player_api.php</code> and a username and password</td><td>Recognises an Xtream login and fills in the server, username and password.</td></tr>
                <tr><td>Just a server address, such as <code>http://line.example.com:8080</code></td><td>Fills in the Xtream server. Add your username and password below it.</td></tr>
                <tr><td>A portal address ending in <code>/c/</code> or <code>portal.php</code></td><td>Switches to Stalker portal. Check the MAC address your provider registered.</td></tr>
                <tr><td>Any other playlist link, such as one ending in <code>.m3u</code> or <code>.m3u8</code></td><td>Adds it as an M3U playlist.</td></tr>
              </tbody>
            </table>
          </div>
          <p>The name is optional. Leave it empty and Aether names the playlist after the provider's address.</p>
          <h3>Try it</h3>
          <p>Paste your link here to see what Aether will do with it. It's checked in your browser and never sent anywhere.</p>
          <LinkPhone client:visible />
        </section>

        <section id="xtream">
          <h2>Xtream Codes</h2>
          <ol class="steps">
            <li>Choose <strong>IPTV Subscription</strong>, then <strong>Xtream</strong>.</li>
            <li>Enter the <strong>server</strong> exactly as your provider gave it, including the port — for example <code>http://line.example.com:8080</code>.</li>
            <li>Enter your <strong>username</strong> and <strong>password</strong>, then tap <strong>Add Playlist</strong>.</li>
          </ol>
          <p>Xtream gives Aether everything at once: live channels with their guide, movies, series and catch-up where your provider offers it.</p>
        </section>

        <section id="m3u">
          <h2>M3U playlist</h2>
          <ol class="steps">
            <li>Choose <strong>IPTV Subscription</strong>, then <strong>M3U</strong>.</li>
            <li>Paste the playlist URL. On iPhone, iPad and Mac you can also import a playlist file instead.</li>
            <li>Tap <strong>Add Playlist</strong>.</li>
          </ol>
          <p>If your provider gives you a separate guide link, add it as described in <a href="#guide">TV guide</a>.</p>
        </section>

        <section id="stalker">
          <h2>Stalker portal</h2>
          <ol class="steps">
            <li>Choose <strong>IPTV Subscription</strong>, then <strong>Stalker</strong>.</li>
            <li>Enter the <strong>portal address</strong> your provider gave you.</li>
            <li>Enter the <strong>MAC address</strong> your provider registered for your subscription, then tap <strong>Add Playlist</strong>.</li>
          </ol>
          <p class="tip"><strong>Note:</strong> Stalker portals hand out short-lived stream links, so movies and episodes from a portal can't be downloaded for offline viewing.</p>
        </section>

        <section id="guide">
          <h2>TV guide (XMLTV)</h2>
          <p>Xtream providers usually include a guide. If yours doesn't, or you prefer another guide, open <span class="path">Settings → TV Guide</span> and add an XMLTV link. You can add several, give each its own update schedule, and refresh one by hand.</p>
        </section>

        <section id="find-server">
          <h2>Finding your server</h2>
          <p>When you choose <strong>Media Server</strong>, Aether looks for Jellyfin, Emby and Plex servers on your Wi-Fi network and lists the ones it finds. Tap one to fill in its address.</p>
          <p>If yours isn't listed, type its address. For an address on your home network without a port, such as <code>192.168.1.20</code>, Aether also tries the usual ports: <code>8096</code> for Jellyfin and Emby, <code>32400</code> for Plex. For a server outside your home, enter the full address, such as <code>https://media.example.com</code>.</p>
          <p class="tip"><strong>Allow local network access.</strong> The first time, iOS asks whether Aether may find devices on your local network. Aether needs that to reach servers at home. If you declined, turn it on in the iPhone's <span class="path">Settings → Privacy &amp; Security → Local Network</span>.</p>
        </section>

        <section id="jellyfin">
          <h2>Jellyfin &amp; Emby</h2>
          <ol class="steps">
            <li>Choose <strong>Media Server</strong> and pick your server, or type its address.</li>
            <li>Enter your <strong>username</strong> and <strong>password</strong> on that server.</li>
            <li>Tap <strong>Add Server</strong>. Aether checks the address and signs in.</li>
          </ol>
          <p>On Jellyfin you can skip the password and sign in with a code instead — see the next section.</p>
        </section>

        <section id="quick-connect">
          <h2>Jellyfin Quick Connect</h2>
          <p>Quick Connect signs you in by approving a short code on a device where you're already signed in to Jellyfin. It's handy on Apple TV, where typing a password with the remote is slow.</p>
          <ol class="steps">
            <li>In Aether, enter the server's address (or pick it from the list), then tap <strong>Sign In with Jellyfin</strong>. Aether shows a code.</li>
            <li>On your phone, computer or another Jellyfin app, open your user menu and choose <strong>Quick Connect</strong>.</li>
            <li>Enter the code and approve it. Aether signs in on its own a moment later.</li>
          </ol>
          <p class="tip"><strong>Quick Connect is off?</strong> The server's administrator turns it on in the Jellyfin dashboard under <span class="path">General</span>. Or sign in with your username and password.</p>
        </section>

        <section id="plex">
          <h2>Plex</h2>
          <ol class="steps">
            <li>Choose <strong>Media Server</strong>, then tap <strong>Sign In with Plex</strong>. Aether shows a code.</li>
            <li>On any device, go to <a href="https://plex.tv/link">plex.tv/link</a> and sign in to your Plex account. On Apple TV you can scan the QR code instead.</li>
            <li>Enter the code. Aether finds your Plex servers and connects.</li>
          </ol>
          <p>You can also type your Plex server's address — for example <code>192.168.1.20:32400</code>.</p>
        </section>

        <section id="silo-webdav">
          <h2>Silo &amp; WebDAV</h2>
          <h3>Silo</h3>
          <p>Enter your Silo server's address and sign in. Aether finds Silo's Jellyfin-compatible service and imports your libraries.</p>
          <h3>WebDAV share</h3>
          <p>Enter the folder's WebDAV address — for example <code>https://nas.example.com/dav/Movies/</code> — with the username and password for the share. Aether walks the folders and recognises movies and episodes from their file names. Subtitle files next to a video (<code>.srt</code>, <code>.vtt</code>, <code>.ass</code>, <code>.sub</code>) and folder artwork such as <code>poster.jpg</code> are picked up too.</p>
        </section>

        <section id="apple-tv">
          <h2>Apple TV</h2>
          <h3>Set up with your iPhone</h3>
          <ol class="steps">
            <li>On the Apple TV's welcome screen, choose <strong>Set Up with iPhone</strong>. A QR code appears.</li>
            <li>Scan it with your iPhone's camera. It opens Aether's add form on the phone — or the App Store, if Aether isn't installed yet.</li>
            <li>Add your provider or server on the iPhone. It appears on the Apple TV by itself, as long as both are signed in to the same iCloud account.</li>
          </ol>
          <h3>Set up on the TV</h3>
          <p>You can also fill in the form with the remote. When a text field is selected, your iPhone offers its keyboard as a notification, which is much quicker than the on-screen keyboard. For Plex and Jellyfin, a sign-in code saves typing a password at all.</p>
        </section>

        <section id="services">
          <h2>Trakt, Simkl &amp; more</h2>
          <p>Optional services live in <span class="path">Settings → Connected Services</span>:</p>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Trakt</strong> and <strong>Simkl</strong> — keep your watch history, progress and watchlists in step. You sign in by entering a code on the service's website, so it works on Apple TV too.</li>
            <li><strong>OpenSubtitles</strong> — search works without an account; sign in with your free account to download subtitles.</li>
            <li><strong>PublicMetaDB</strong> — sync history and progress, and use community skip times, with an API key from publicmetadb.com.</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section id="profiles">
          <h2>Profiles &amp; parental controls</h2>
          <p>Each person can have their own profile with separate watch history, progress and favourites, in <span class="path">Settings → Profiles</span>. Mark a profile as a child's to hide restricted categories from browsing and search, and lock sensitive sections behind a PIN in <strong>Parental Controls</strong>.</p>
          <p>Still stuck? See <a href="/support/#troubleshooting">troubleshooting</a> or <a href="/support/">get in touch</a>.</p>
        </section>
      </div>
    </section>

  <script>
    // Highlights the guide section you're reading in the table of contents.
    const links = new Map(
      [...document.querySelectorAll<HTMLAnchorElement>(".toc a")].map((link) => [link.hash.slice(1), link]),
    );
    const observer = new IntersectionObserver(
      (entries) => {
        for (const entry of entries) {
          if (!entry.isIntersecting) continue;
          links.forEach((link) => link.classList.remove("is-active"));
          links.get(entry.target.id)?.classList.add("is-active");
        }
      },
      { rootMargin: "-20% 0px -70% 0px" },
    );
    links.forEach((_, id) => {
      const section = document.getElementById(id);
      if (section) observer.observe(section);
    });
  </script>
</Base>
